<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-WMC nickel workers not to take action.</title>
<headline>RTRS-WMC nickel workers not to take action.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Unionised workers at WMC Ltd's Kambalda gold/nickel complex in Western Australia plan no immediate industrial action following the company's decision to lay off more than half the 800-strong workforce at the site, an official of the Australian Workers Union (AWU) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;The company may have been ready for an industrial action on our part, although the workers decided not to take any action,&quot; AWU branch secretary Glen Anderton told Reuters.</p>
</text>
